  "baseRefOid": "5996f9043c27bafa90b23e1c937de92a738f1a76",
  "body": "\u03ba = 0.00162128508944984 (conservative \u03ba = 0.001621285086572193)\n\nThis PR independently replays the exact head of CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#604, a new cold_end architecture that lets 14 factory-scratch helpers per provider call finish at dimension-4 frames after an exact premix and guarded multi-gate cleanup. It records the fresh evidence without changing any published upstream head.\n\nEvidence:\n\n- 55/55 top-level stages passed from the pinned PR604 head in 601.33 seconds, with no reused local outputs.\n- The audit independently checked all 55 stage-log hashes and all 54 receipt-artifact hashes, then checked the package manifest and SPEC hash.\n- ck\u00d744, atm3\u00d722 and jp8\u00d76 providers pass actual scalar words, arbitrary dirty restoration in both orientations, both reflected ledgers, native frames, wrappers, phase edges, owners, fresh invoice, both moment engines, exact assembly and negative controls.\n- The fresh profile is {1:185792, 2:32576, 3:23600, 4:14128, 5:5040, 6:2016, 8:576, 32:1, 48:2094}.\n\nThe full receipt, result, assembly controls, phase controls, owner/profile audit and independent audit summary are in certificates/pr604-independent-replay/. The replay remains conditional on the inherited all-size compiler, common-label/mutable-source realization, whole-call hosting, precision/tape/exact recovery, analytic transfer and bit H1\u2013H5 assumptions. No Lean replay or unconditional theorem is claimed.\n\nProvenance and AI disclosure: the upstream cold_end construction is credited to DreamingOfClouds with Claude Opus 5.5 assistance and its inherited contributors. This independent replay and certificate packaging were prepared with OpenAI Codex assistance.\n",
  "commits": [
    {
      "authoredDate": "2026-10-08T02:22:42Z",
      "authors": [
        {
          "email": "eumemic@gmail.com",
          "id": "U_kgDOBaipYw",
