          "login": "claude",
          "name": "Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context)"
        }
      ],
      "committedDate": "2026-10-08T02:22:42Z",
      "messageBody": "Replace the complex motif's per-pair side wires with a shared-sum circuit\n(3,693,800 -> 108,195 side roles per invocation at h=25). Binary coordinate\nand pair-star labels give every frame residual an orthonormal basis; injected\ndisjoint pieces must leave an outside point uncovered, since otherwise the\nresidual is an alternating hyperbolic plane.\n\nThe certified complex saving rises from 418/10^12 to 14/10^9, so the paired\nbit network becomes the only binding motif. With the compact-control\nrecurrence this gives the conditional witness kappa = 59/10^11 > 2^-31,\n590/83 (about 7.11) times the preceding 83/10^12.\n\n- scripts/complex_circuit.py: circuit, F2 label algebra, role compiler,\n  both-direction frame checks, exact dirty-scratch simulator\n- scripts/complex_network.py: full h=25 checks, counts, guard, gate bound,\n  parameter witness -> certificates/complex-network.json\n- scripts/make_complex_circuit_patch.py -> patches/complex-circuit-31.patch\n- notes/complex-circuit-*.tex and artifacts/complex-circuit-note.pdf\n- tests/test_complex_network.py; README, status and reproducibility docs\n\nContributed by eumemic.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "messageHeadline": "feat: compress complex network for kappa 59/10^11",
      "oid": "17a50d7d1fd00cd1b57e45d4ceee98e2dfada95f"
    },
