      ],
      "committedDate": "2026-10-08T04:08:50Z",
      "messageBody": "- Evaluate the Gaussian maps S' and E as chirped block correlations\n  with the established multiplier: O(p^(1+delta)) per output\n- Bound powers of the resampling correction by a potential argument,\n  so the Neumann series needs O(p/alpha^2 + 1/theta) terms\n- alpha = floor(sqrt(b/(8d))): Gaussian cost O(d^2 p^delta), epsilon\n  may approach 1/2; beta = 19/25 fits the compressed complex saving\n- Conditional witness kappa = 1479/10^12 > 2^-30 (1479/590 above 59/10^11)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "messageHeadline": "feat: fast Gaussian resampling for kappa 1479/10^12",
      "oid": "d3d370c34937503bd3fa63c83d505a05e8e50893"
    },
